			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu/116461673466023953",
			"author": {
				"name": "Thibault D.",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/734/800/021/512/545/original/63e74fa542b78169.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T20:55:09.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>khalidabuhakmeh</span></a></span> Good piece. I have very similar thoughts and feelings.</p><p>. This is a management failure, management should not just push AI usage forward for the shake of AI usage but should also (together with the team) create strategies about what we want AI to do and what we don't want AI to do. Just because AI _can_ do something does not mean we want to delegate it to it. We have to discuss what we want our jobs to be. \"You make meaning through the doing.\" 💯&nbsp;</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116461676590194486",
			"parentId": "116461673970086725",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu/116461676484503296",
			"author": {
				"name": "Thibault D.",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/734/800/021/512/545/original/63e74fa542b78169.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T20:55:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>khalidabuhakmeh</span></a></span> <br>. How do we raise concerns about AI risks when the answer is always \"more AI\", \"AI will fix this\"? Merging bugs, merging 12000lines is OK, AI will fix it. Too much code to read? AI will summarize it. Merge conflicts skyrocketing? AI will fix.</p><p>I feel a lot like the author on most examples</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116461715322920026",
			"parentId": "116461676590194486",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu/116461715288030836",
			"author": {
				"name": "Thibault D.",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/734/800/021/512/545/original/63e74fa542b78169.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T21:05:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>khalidabuhakmeh</span></a></span> I wonder if GenAI isn't the nuclear weapons of our industry. We can build it and we can use it, but we may soon find out we shouldn't.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116461733281288754",
			"parentId": "116461715322920026",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh/116461733241708200",
			"author": {
				"name": "Khalid ⚡",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T21:10:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ThibaultDu</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I think most folks using AI have artifact derangement syndrome. </p><p>Focusing on the outputs but losing the intangibles that get you better outcomes.</p><p>Sure, AI can give you a result, but it robs you of what would have otherwise been an educational and intrinsically worthwhile journey.</p><p>It's a Faustian deal every time. For some, it's worth it, for others not so much. I think folks need to grapple with that.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116461747799098931",
			"parentId": "116461733281288754",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh/116461747698228148",
			"author": {
				"name": "Khalid ⚡",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/296/176/354/255/607/original/70d4899634530145.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T21:14:01.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ThibaultDu</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> the other insidious part of it is we've all been trained to put our identities into our work. It gives us purpose.</p><p>For some, they see AI as a means of accelerating their worth.</p><p>Others see AI output for what it is, artifacts. Material in a Material world. It's hollow \"content\", and adds nothing to their feelings of self-worth or identity.</p><p>My concern is for folks building an identity on shaky premises.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "116461752688148805",
			"parentId": "116461733281288754",
