				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ThibaultDu",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/734/800/021/512/545/original/63e74fa542b78169.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-04-24T21:33:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@khalidabuhakmeh\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>khalidabuhakmeh</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I agree 100%. I just chose to work under the hypothesis that GenAI _does_ yield efficiency gains to ask \"even then, is that how you want to work?\". But I agree that in the long run there are many issues with sustaining this way of working.</p>",
